.* SETUPBCKUP: the task menu that sets up the backups.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='SETUPBCKUP'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='CMD CALL QCMD'.F9=Command line
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=SETUPBCKUP HELP=HLPSETUPBCKUP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Set Up Backup
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.To select one of the following, type its number below and press Enter:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD ?CHGBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*DAILY)'.Change daily backup options
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD ?CHGBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*WEEKLY)'.Change weekly backup options
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?CHGBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*MONTHLY)'.Change monthly backup options
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD DSPBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*DAILY)'.Display daily backup options
:MENUI OPTION=20 ACTION='CMD ?ADDJOBSCDE JOB(QEZBCKUP) CMD(RUNBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*DAILY)) FRQ(*WEEKLY) SCDDAY(*ALL)'.Schedule the daily backup
:EMENU.
:BOTINST.Type a menu option below
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPSETUPBCKUP.Set Up Backup - Help
:P.Options 1 to 3 change what each backup saves, where it goes and how it
runs. Option 10 shows the daily options; option 20 adds a job schedule
entry that runs the daily backup each day.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter. F9 opens a command line, F3
leaves the menu and F12 returns to the one before it.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
